      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T08:30:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003emap\u003ckey, Ref\u003cRootSignature\u003e\u003e with RootSignature being our new object that contains info about the D3D12 root signature.\n\nThat would be an option. Structure would be clear if we define a new \"RootSignature\" for all native backends. It lives between GPUPipelineLayout and GPUPipeline and stores real backend rootsignature. Pipeline holds it for querying some info. (And it could hold commandRootSignature). What\u0027s more, this \"rootsignature\" could be held in PipelineBase and BindGroupStateTrackers.\n\nConsidering the change size to address the complete design and the truth that we have limited internal immediate data, another option would be we keep current implementation for now (waste some immediate data slots but keeps the structure clean) :).",
